# Git workflow

- ALWAYS commit every code/notebook change you make in this session, in a coherent message, without being asked. Do not ask for permission to commit.
- ALWAYS push immediately after committing, also without asking. Push to the **current branch** (`git push -u origin HEAD`) -- only push to `main` when the working branch IS `main`. Never auto-push a feature/experiment branch to `main`.
- When committing, stage ONLY the files you actually changed this turn. Do not blanket-add unrelated untracked files lying around in the working tree.
- This shell is PowerShell: do NOT use `&&`, `||`, or heredocs (`<<'EOF'`). Chain commands with `;`, and pass multi-line commit messages via `git commit -F <file>`.
